preConditionHook:
// A GAP THAT HAS NOT FILLED (G03-34, "are there gaps up that do not fill").
// The bar fillLookback bars ago gapped in the trade's direction -- its whole
// range sat clear of the bar gapBarOffset bars before it, TrueGapBar's own
// non-overlap relation -- and no bar since has traded back into it: the LOWEST
// LOW of the fillLookback bars since is still above the pre-gap bar's high. The
// short mirrors: a gap DOWN whose highest high since is still below the pre-gap
// bar's low.
//
// MECHANIZED AT A FIXED LAG rather than by scanning backwards for the most
// recent gap, which keeps it a plain window rule; the scanned form is
// GapFilledExit's construction and is the recorded alternative. fillLookback
// therefore does double duty by construction: it is BOTH how many bars ago the
// gap printed AND the span of the not-filled test, and those are the same set
// of bars -- Lowest(Low, fillLookback) covers offsets 0..fillLookback-1,
// exactly the bars after the gap bar.
//
// gapBarOffset is the SPAN OF THE NON-OVERLAP TEST: at the default 1 it is
// TrueGapBar's relation (the gap bar clear of the bar immediately before it),
// and a larger value asks the gap bar to stand clear of an earlier bar instead.
//
// NOT GapHoldsAbovePriorSessionClose, whose reference is the PRIOR SESSION's
// close and which needs the session machinery; this reference is a BAR gap, so
// it works on any bar scale and is what Grimes asks for on a daily chart. NOT
// GapFilledExit, an Exit anchored to a scanned-for gap. NOT
// PostGapFadeBlockWindow, which asks only whether ANY gap printed in a window
// and carries no fill test.
//
// SHIFT TEST: every term is a price compared with a price from the same series.
//
// The window scan mirrors EasyLanguage's Extremes(), which Highest()/Lowest()
// call: seeded at the window's first bar (offset 0), scanning the rest with a
// STRICT comparison so a tie keeps the earliest bar. Extremes is EL SOURCE, so
// its comparisons carry the relational tolerance and use el_lt / el_gt.
//
// Scratch below is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope, so the hooks
// survive a double placement; every one is fully assigned each bar before it is
// read.
gapHi = high[fillLookback + gapBarOffset];
gapLo = low[fillLookback + gapBarOffset];
sinceLo = low[0];
sinceHi = high[0];
for (int i = 1; i < (int)fillLookback; ++i) {
    if (el_lt(low[i], sinceLo)) sinceLo = low[i];
    if (el_gt(high[i], sinceHi)) sinceHi = high[i];
}
